{
	title: 'read_url tool: a web page as readable text',
	spec: 'A `read_url` model tool (src/host/tools/read_url.ts, tool name read_url) fetches one http(s) URL and returns readable text. Other schemes are an error result and fetch nothing. HTML becomes simple text: scripts, styles and markup dropped, block elements as line breaks, entities decoded, runs of blank lines collapsed; the page title first. Plain text and JSON pass through. An image (png, jpeg, gif, webp) comes back as an image part the model sees, within the attachment size cap. Any other content type is saved under paths.fileDir (/tmp/hal/file/) and the result gives its path, type and size so bash can open it. Output is capped like read (50k chars) with a note of how much was cut. Redirects are followed; a non-2xx status is an error result with the status; a 30 s timeout and the turn abort signal cancel. Stdlib only: no HTML parser dependency. Artifact old-read-url.ts (reference). Tests with a local Bun.serve: HTML to text, the scheme check, the cap, an image part, a binary saved to a file.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Tool results keep fetched images as session blob references (image field), not embedded base64 in history; provider adapters replay image data from the blob. paths.fileDir() with no name is the download directory; with a name remains the pasted-file path. HTML is handled with a small regex/entity pass. Startup timing test can fail under parallel builds; other tests, tsc and lint passed.'
	],
	needs: ['sj']
}
